Z||000000||fotofrank||09-02-2000||02:42 PM||||I have a Holley TBI P/N 500-1. It is installed and works ok. However I got it used and donot have any documatation for it. Does it have an ajustable fuel regulator? Are there any adjustments/options that improve it's performance? I have also heard that a "spacer" can boost performance. Is this true and how does it work?<P>------------------<BR>Peace and Happiness<BR>Frank and his fotoflash, an '84 SE 2M4<BR>http://fotofrank.homestead.com/fiero.html||||reg||5
Z||000001||Fearless Freep||09-02-2000||03:11 PM||||On the top of the TBI, there is a small place that looks like a small hole that has been filled in.....Underneath that small metal plug (you will have to drill it out) is a screw that will help with mild idle adjustments.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Patrick's Dad||09-02-2000||09:07 PM||||Going to take a shot at this one....<P>Spacing the TBI should be like spacing a carb or lengthening the intake runners on a "traditional" FI engine; it increases horsepower, but (I think I remember this, someone correct me if I'm wrong) at the expense of low end pulling power (torque). Many apps have "dual plane" intakes (I'm looking at this for my 318 Plymouth). The shorter intake runner is for torque and the longer one for increased hp. Olds used a dual runner on its 190hp Quad 4 years ago, which (again, I think that I remember this) used a butterfly valve to open the longer runners at high rpm.<P>I think that this is also why Pontiac designed the Fiero's intake plenum the way it is, rather than straight runners to the valvetrain.<P>Open to correction....||||reg||1
Z||000003||88formula||09-02-2000||09:59 PM||||You got it backwards Patrick. Longer intake runners foster low-end torque at the expense of upper end power. Tuned port injection has long runners; this is what the fiero 2.8 has. Shorter intake runners don't provide good low-end toque but do give better upper end power than longer runners do.||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||09-03-2000||02:47 PM||||The aftermarket holley TBI should not have a plugged idle adjust. It has a bigger bore & butterfly but otherwise it is the same as the OE unit. It is adjusted and maintained the same ways. ||||reg||1
